// pf_facade_in.vfl - B4's INPUT ADAPTER.  PRIM wrangle over the mass's CAP
// faces, which are already the footprint loop of their own volume.
//
// polyChain's facade port (`facade.footprint_loops`) asks for exactly three
// things: one CLOSED footprint per primitive, prim `pc_height`, prim
// `pc_array`.  B2 already emits all three under different names, so B4 is an
// adapter and not a builder - which is `citygen_buildings.md` §0.0a's own
// prediction ("B4 may be largely polyChain CONFIGURATION, not new code").
//
// ⚠️ THE CAP IS THE LOOP, AND IT IS THE LOOP AT THE WRONG HEIGHT.  `pfb_cell`
// builds the cap as the plan walked CCW at `ytop`; a facade is built UPWARD
// from its footprint, so the loop has to come back down to the floor datum.
// `pf_plinth_top` is that datum - the ONE level for the whole building - so
// the facade starts where the plinth ends and not at the bottom of a skirt
// that follows the ground.
//
// ⚠️ A PRIM WRANGLE WRITING POINT POSITIONS DOUBLE-WRITES ANY SHARED POINT
// (houdini-procedural-modeling §6), and the reason it is safe here is a fact
// about the input rather than a hope: `pfb_cell` mints its own `top[]` points
// per cell, and the blast upstream keeps only the caps - so after it every
// point on this stream is referenced by exactly one prim.  Each point is
// written once, with its own prim's datum.
//
// ⚠️ WINDING IS NOT CHECKED HERE and does not need to be.  `pfb_cell`
// canonicalises every cell to CCW in (x,z) before it builds anything, and
// that is the winding polyChain's own 2D fixtures are authored in
// (`cases2d.L_FOOTPRINT`); its array frame's up axis flips if a loop arrives
// the other way.
float base = f@pf_plinth_top;
int pts[] = primpoints(0, @primnum);
// ⚠️ TYPED LOCAL FIRST.  `point()` returns an untyped value, so `max(...)` and
// `.y` on it are AMBIGUOUS and the wrangle refuses to compile - the dev-loop
// trap list's own first VEX entry, hit five separate times in one session
// before it was written down.
float ytop = -1e18;
foreach (int pt; pts) {
    vector q = point(0, "P", pt);
    ytop = max(ytop, q.y);
}

f@pc_height = ytop - base;
s@pc_array = s@pf_volume_id;

foreach (int pt; pts) {
    vector p = point(0, "P", pt);
    setpointattrib(0, "P", pt, set(p.x, base, p.z));
}
